WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.444
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.744 --> 00:00:14.590
Unit twenty-eight: Emotions and Regrets. In this unit, you will describe feelings and talk about wishes.

4
00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:16.399
regret.

5
00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:20.538
regret means a feeling of sadness about something you did or didn't do.

6
00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:23.244
My only regret is that I didn't learn to swim.

7
00:00:23.944 --> 00:00:26.039
Your turn. Say: regret.

8
00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:29.624
regret.

9
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:31.502
overwhelmed.

10
00:00:32.202 --> 00:00:35.699
overwhelmed means having too many feelings or tasks to deal with.

11
00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:38.486
She felt overwhelmed by all her exams.

12
00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:41.664
Your turn. Say: overwhelmed.

13
00:00:44.364 --> 00:00:45.400
overwhelmed.

14
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:47.336
calm down.

15
00:00:48.036 --> 00:00:51.441
calm down means to become less angry, upset or excited.

16
00:00:51.741 --> 00:00:53.497
Take a deep breath and calm down.

17
00:00:54.197 --> 00:00:56.501
Your turn. Say: calm down.

18
00:00:59.201 --> 00:01:00.213
calm down.

19
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:01.986
mood.

20
00:01:02.686 --> 00:01:05.324
mood means the way you feel at a particular time.

21
00:01:05.624 --> 00:01:07.054
He's in a good mood today.

22
00:01:07.754 --> 00:01:09.768
Your turn. Say: mood.

23
00:01:12.468 --> 00:01:13.249
mood.

24
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.135
emotional.

25
00:01:15.835 --> 00:01:18.392
emotional means showing strong feelings.

26
00:01:18.692 --> 00:01:20.680
The wedding speech was very emotional.

27
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.417
Your turn. Say: emotional.

28
00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:27.234
emotional.

29
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.181
resentful.

30
00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:33.065
resentful means feeling angry because of unfair treatment.

31
00:01:33.365 --> 00:01:35.841
He felt resentful when his colleague got the promotion.

32
00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:38.856
Your turn. Say: resentful.

33
00:01:41.556 --> 00:01:42.569
resentful.

34
00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:44.410
delighted.

35
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.296
delighted means very pleased and happy.

36
00:01:47.596 --> 00:01:49.363
We were delighted with the result.

37
00:01:50.063 --> 00:01:52.274
Your turn. Say: delighted.

38
00:01:54.974 --> 00:01:55.778
delighted.

39
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.692
heartbroken.

40
00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:01.599
heartbroken means extremely sad, usually because of a loss.

41
00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:03.968
She was heartbroken when her dog died.

42
00:02:04.668 --> 00:02:07.018
Your turn. Say: heartbroken.

43
00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:10.882
heartbroken.

44
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.987
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.287 --> 00:02:17.590
I feel overwhelmed. I wish I had more time to study.

46
00:02:18.883 --> 00:02:21.524
Calm down. What's making you feel this way?

47
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:26.653
I have three exams next week. I wish I didn't have so many.

48
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.984
Do you have any regrets about this term?

49
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:35.399
I wish I were more organised. My mood changes so quickly.

50
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:39.463
Make a plan. You'll be delighted with the results.

51
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.736
Grammar focus: wish + past simple.

52
00:02:44.036 --> 00:02:48.567
Use wish plus past simple to talk about present situations we want to be different.

53
00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:51.691
For example: I wish I had more free time.

54
00:02:51.991 --> 00:02:55.407
In formal English, use were: I wish I were more organised.

55
00:02:55.707 --> 00:03:00.725
Use were for all persons in formal English: I wish I were, he wishes he were.

56
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:04.613
Now read and listen. Managing Big Emotions.

57
00:03:04.913 --> 00:03:07.922
Everyone feels overwhelmed or resentful sometimes.

58
00:03:09.217 --> 00:03:12.575
Psychologists say that naming your emotions helps you calm down.

59
00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:17.032
Writing in a journal can improve your mood in just ten minutes.

60
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:21.257
Many people wish they talked about their feelings more often.

61
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:26.012
Sharing a regret with a friend can turn a heavy feeling into a lighter one.

62
00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:29.853
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:30.153 --> 00:03:33.163
Feeling angry because of unfair treatment is blank.

64
00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:36.826
A, delighted. B, resentful. C, emotional.

65
00:03:40.817 --> 00:03:43.269
The answer is B: resentful.

66
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:47.970
I wish I blank a car. I have to take the bus every day.

67
00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.494
A, have. B, had. C, would have.

68
00:03:55.483 --> 00:03:56.984
The answer is B: had.

69
00:03:58.483 --> 00:04:00.553
He wishes he blank more confident.

70
00:04:00.853 --> 00:04:03.531
A, is. B, were. C, be.

71
00:04:07.517 --> 00:04:09.354
The answer is B: were.

72
00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.221
Extremely sad because of a loss is blank.

73
00:04:13.521 --> 00:04:17.767
A, heartbroken. B, calm down. C, mood.

74
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.831
The answer is A: heartbroken.

75
00:04:25.317 --> 00:04:28.152
According to the text, what helps you calm down?

76
00:04:28.452 --> 00:04:32.570
A, naming your emotions. B, drinking coffee. C, staying alone.

77
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:38.827
The answer is A: naming your emotions.

78
00:04:40.317 --> 00:04:44.397
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you wish were different in your life right now?

79
00:04:49.697 --> 00:04:54.448
I wish I had more time for my hobbies, and I wish I were better at managing stress.

80
00:04:54.748 --> 00:04:56.330
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:04:57.317 --> 00:05:01.234
Great work today! You learned eight new words and wish + past simple.

82
00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.663
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

83
00:05:04.963 --> 00:05:07.522
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

84
00:05:07.822 --> 00:05:10.881
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

